  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-250002912</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming Vegetable Markets - A learning pilot to demonstrate cost-effective impact at scale in smallholder vegetable production</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Led by East-West Seed Knowledge Transfer, in partnership with SeedNL and Wageningen Plant Research, the pilot positions vegetables as a business opportunity for smallholder farmer communities that, as yet, operate outside developed markets. Using (pre commercial) market-based approaches to connect informed farmers to open markets, the pilot will test and prove an approach to deliver scale in cost effective and replicable ways.
The primary focus will be on farmer income through increased sales of a variety of safe-to-eat vegetables, produced under sustainable and climate-smart practices for local and regional wet markets. For every USD 40 per farmer invested in training, farmers are expected to gain on average USD 253 in additional annual net income. With 150,000 farmers, this will result in a combined increase of approximately USD 38 million per year. In addition, the pilot will generate enough affordable, and safe-to-eat vegetables to supply three million lower-income consumers</narrative>
  </description>
